 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-016\", \"clauses\": {\"illustrate\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"reasoning\": \"F17 is the only family whose text names the illustrating act, shading a shape. Its fraction_str slot is nested from F08, F20 and F21. F08 yields the in-scope unit fractions, so the clause is producible. F17 also carries the out-of-scope fault named in failing_families.\"}, \"half\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"{num}/{den}\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 with num member 1 and den member 2 prints the one-half form in correct_answer and format_data.mcq_options. Both members are drawn from the declared lists.\"}, \"quarter\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"{num}/{den}\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 with num member 1 and den member 4 prints the one-quarter form in correct_answer and format_data.mcq_options. The den members are drawn from the grade denom_pool.\"}, \"parts_of_whole\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F04\", \"template\": \"A {frac_lbl} shows how many equal parts are shaded out of the total.\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 is a hint that states the part-of-a-whole relation: equal parts, shaded, out of the total. Its frac_lbl slot is nested from F02, which prints the vocabulary word fraction.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F17\", \"F20\", \"F21\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"{numer}/{denom}\", \"{unshaded}/{denom}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"The competency names only the one-half and one-quarter fractions. F20 (template {numer}/{denom}, correct_answer) has its numer and denom slots drawn from an arithmetic domain derived from denominator and numerator, with no bound to a numerator of 1. Subtracting the numerator from the denominator gives 3 at denominator 4, so the keyed answer can be a fraction the competency does not name. F21 (template {unshaded}/{denom}, correct_answer and distractors) has the same unbounded arithmetic. F17 (template Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.) nests F20 and F21 in fraction_str, so the question text can ask a learner to shade a fraction outside the lc's scope. This is content beyond the competency's explicit scope under Content Rule 3. The declared_bounds entry for unit_fraction is not reflected in these domains, so the judgment rests on the domains as printed. Not failing: F16 and F12 can produce a distractor equal to the keyed value. reason_kinds assigns arithmetic correctness to the hint contract and §1E, so I did not count it here. F06 and F07 print their label twice (for example bottom number in parentheses after the nested label). That is redundant but not wrong, so I did not count it either. F11 includes the number line and set model variants. I did not count them as out of scope.\"}",
